## Proposed answer:
To ensure active LDP /32 prefixes are advertised to a BGP neighbor using RFC 3107 label encoding, even if other BGP routes exist for the same prefix, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "your-group-name"
        neighbor "neighbor-ip-address"
            family label-ipv4
            advertise-ldp-prefix
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**
1. `family label-ipv4` enables labeled-unicast IPv4 support for the neighbor.
2. `advertise-ldp-prefix` forces advertisement of active LDP /32 prefixes with RFC 3107 labels, overriding any existing BGP routes for the same prefix.
3. Replace `your-group-name` and `neighbor-ip-address` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP.

This configuration ensures only **active** LDP FEC prefixes (those forwarding traffic) are advertised using the legacy RFC 3107 standard.
