To configure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR to aggregate link capacity metrics from external IPv4 peers for improved load sharing, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <your_ebgp_group_name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<your_ebgp_group_name>` with your actual EBGP group name. These commands:
1. Enable link bandwidth handling for the BGP group
2. Accept link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
3. Sum the bandwidth values of active multipaths for each prefix

After applying this configuration, BGP will:
- Process received link-bandwidth attributes from EBGP peers
- Calculate the total bandwidth across all active paths for each prefix
- Use this aggregated metric for load-sharing decisions on IPv4 routes
