To ensure IPv6 traffic streams remain stable during routing protocol issues on your Nokia 7750 SR, configure BFD for rapid failure detection and Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) to maintain IPv6 routes during control-plane disruptions. Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ipv6-address>` with your specific values:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "<group-name>"
        family ipv6
        bfd-enable
        graceful-restart
            long-lived
                family ipv6
                exit
            exit
        exit
        neighbor <neighbor-ipv6-address>
            family ipv6
            bfd-enable
            graceful-restart
                long-lived
                    family ipv6
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key actions:**
1. **`family ipv6`** enables IPv6 route exchange at group and neighbor levels.
2. **`bfd-enable`** accelerates failure detection to prevent session drops during transient issues.
3. **LLGR for IPv6** (`graceful-restart > long-lived > family ipv6`) retains stale routes during control-plane delays, maintaining traffic flow without resetting sessions.

Apply this configuration to relevant BGP groups/neighbors handling your IPv6 traffic.
