```console
configure router
    bgp
        group "GROUP-NAME"
            local-address "core-link-1"
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- Replace `"GROUP-NAME"` with your actual BGP group name
- The `local-address` command under the BGP group forces all peers in that group to source BGP sessions using the IP address assigned to the **core-link-1** interface
- This configuration applies to all neighbors in the group simultaneously, eliminating per-neighbor configuration

**Verification:**  
After committing the configuration, check session source addresses with:
```console
show router bgp summary
```
