To enable the Nokia 7750 SR to accept dynamically pushed inbound filtering preferences (via BGP ORF) from a specific BGP neighbor, use the following CLI configuration. Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your actual group and neighbor IP values:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            outbound-route-filtering
                extended-community
                    accept-orf
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key Details:
- **`outbound-route-filtering`**: Enables BGP Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) capability negotiation.
- **`extended-community`**: Specifies extended community-based ORF filters (required for `accept-orf`).
- **`accept-orf`**: Directs the router to honor filters pushed by the neighbor during session negotiation.

This configuration ensures the router dynamically accepts and applies the neighbor's requested inbound filters.
