To set the BGP hold-time to a maximum of 2 minutes while allowing negotiation down to 1 minute, use the following CLI configuration:

```console
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            hold-time 120 min 60
```

**Key details:**  
- The `hold-time 120` sets your proposed hold-time to 120 seconds (2 minutes).  
- The `min 60` ensures your router accepts peer-proposed hold-times as low as 60 seconds (1 minute).  
- The negotiated hold-time will be the **lowest value** acceptable to both peers (e.g., if the peer proposes 90 seconds, the session uses 90 seconds).  

**Note:** Apply this at the neighbor, group, or global BGP level depending on your peer scope. The keepalive timer automatically adjusts to one-third of the negotiated hold-time (e.g., 40 seconds for 120 seconds, 20 seconds for 60 seconds).
