To configure BGP Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) for specific services while excluding the forwarding (F) flag for regular IPv4/IPv6 unicast, apply the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        family l2-vpn
            advertised-stale-time 600
        exit
        family flow-ipv4
            advertised-stale-time 600
        exit
        family flow-ipv6
            advertised-stale-time 600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
- **`long-lived`**: Enables LLGR context to configure extended stale route preservation.
- **`family`**: Specifies the address families (L2-VPN, flow-IPv4, flow-IPv6) that will preserve stale routes during restart. Regular IPv4/IPv6 unicast families are **excluded** to avoid setting the F flag.
- **`advertised-stale-time 600`**: Sets the stale route preservation time to 600 seconds (adjust as needed) for the specified families. This ensures peers retain these routes during the restart. 

This configuration explicitly enables LLGR only for L2-VPN and flow-IP services, preventing the F flag from being set for excluded IPv4/IPv6 unicast routes.
